{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":293649,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d69e72fe-090a-45e1-97ca-105ad4da7107","total_cost_usd":1.2104789999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61228,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"output_tokens":21703,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61228,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":21703,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61228},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45178,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.045278000000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":21703,"cacheReadInputTokens":20672,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61228,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.165201,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"playtester\",\n  \"verdict\": \"targets_missed\",\n  \"summary\": \"Flown, this configuration never reaches orbit at all, its cheapest descent is a single plunge in all nine band-and-load cases, and no world in the 324-config grid satisfies all eight design targets — the reentry rules need the GDD's own fallbacks and a smaller, denser planet, not a nudge to the ablation constants.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ascent_fails_every_band\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.6\",\n      \"claim\": \"The params assert 1495 m/s of total Delta-v against roughly 1150 m/s to circularise in the suborbital band, leaving ~300 m/s of skim-shaping margin, at a liftoff TWR of 2.19.\",\n      \"measured\": \"All three ascents failed: suborbital, low and high all report reached=false, why='crashed on ascent', fuel_remaining_kg=0, fuel_margin_pct=0. The exploration grid says this is fixable — bands_reachable is satisfied by 0.5 of 324 configs and fuel_margin_sane by 0.25 — but every config in the top 12 has radius_m=60000, not the baseline's 250000. Every descent number in the verification sweep was therefore flown from an orbit the ship cannot actually reach.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"no_world_satisfies_all_targets\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"4.5\",\n      \"claim\": \"The design asserts that reachable bands, aerobraking that cools, a survivable unstaged braking pass, a soft full-hold landing and a difficulty curve that rises with band can all hold at once.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Across 324 worlds the best score is 7 of 8 and max_score=8 is never reached. In the reported top 12, skimming_cools_the_entry and unstaged_pass_survivable are mutually exclusive: the four 7/8 configs that survive an unstaged pass measure skim multipliers of [1, 0.985, 0.971, 0.958] to [1, 0.993, 0.987, 0.982] — skimming does essentially nothing — while the one 7/8 config where skimming works ([1, 0.801, 0.299, 0.299]) burns to 339 peak heat unstaged. Satisfaction rates: unstaged_pass_survivable 0.111, full_hold_lands_soft 0.29, difficulty_rises_with_band 0.383, skimming_cools_the_entry 0.451.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"unstaged_braking_not_survivable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"GDD 2.3.1 makes pre-stage braking the intended descent: shallow passes with the naked hull soaking slow heat while thrust remains to shape periapsis, with unstaged_heat_multiplier=3 and cargo damage only beginning at 100% heat.\",\n      \"measured\": \"unstaged_braking reports a shallow suborbital pass at 397 peak heat and a shallow low-band pass at 112, both survivable=false against heat_capacity=100. It is the least achievable target in the whole grid — 0.111 of 324 worlds — and the four grid configs that do achieve it all lose the skimming benefit to do so. This is a rule that no tuning of the current knobs reaches.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ablation_optimum_is_one_pass\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.optimal_skims asserts 0 / 1 / 2 skims for suborbital / low / high, with cost_curve high = [40.16, 36.43, 35.67, 38.41] — a U with its floor at two skims — and GDD 4.5 risk 1 asks the cheapest descent to be 2-4 committed passes, never a single plunge.\",\n      \"measured\": \"cheapest_pass_count = 1 in all nine band-and-load cases, and ablation is monotone increasing in pass count everywhere. High band, full hold: [19.6, 28.6, 30.5, 31.5, 32.3, 33.0, 33.5, 35.1, ...] rising to 40.1 at 20 passes — the shape and the level both disagree with the authored curve. Suborbital empty runs 8.5 -> 11.5 across 1-5 passes, low full hold 21.7 -> 35.0. The U-curve does not exist as flown: skim cooling saturates (grid rate 0.889, and suborbital measures [1, 0.742, 0.742, 0.742] — flat after one skim) while cycle_toll_growth=1.9 compounds, so no k>1 can ever pay for itself. GDD 4.5 risk 1 is confirmed, not cleared.\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocking\",\n      \"kind\": \"design\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skim_shaping_unaffordable\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The descent is k shallow skims at one periapsis then a committed entry at a deeper one, with the burn between them paid out of the ~300 m/s the params reserve as skim-shaping margin.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The commit burn costs 51-53 m/s per skim from the low band and 46-49 m/s from the high band at entry_depth 0 (18-36 m/s at the shallowest sampled depth), so a three-skim descent needs roughly 140-160 m/s. Measured fuel_margin_pct is 0 in every band because the ascent never completes, so multi-pass aerobraking is currently unfunded even where it is physically reachable.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"heat_capacity_exceeded_at_base_tier\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"heat_capacity=100 is described as a gate calibrated so a full low-band hold flown direct peaks at exactly 100 and a full suborbital hold sits comfortably below it; heat shield upgrades buy margin, not immunity.\",\n      \"measured\": \"Every full-hold descent exceeds the gate on its own cheapest trajectory: 112 (suborbital), 106 (low), 102 (high). Half hold reads 93 / 89 / 85 and empty 71 / 67 / 64. In the depth-controlled skims block the overshoot is worse: an empty ship direct from the low band peaks at 127.4 and only reaches 101 after three skims; empty from the high band peaks at 158.6 and is still at 140.2 after three. A full hold from the starting band with the starting shield begins damaging cargo, which breaks the opening loop rather than gating the top of it.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"skim_multipliers_wrong_and_band_inverted\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier is a single global array [1, 0.94, 0.90, 0.88], flagged by its author as a guess pending measurement.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The measured arrays are band-specific and none matches: suborbital [1, 0.742, 0.742, 0.742], low [1, 0.937, 0.869, 0.791], high [1, 0.96, 0.92, 0.882]. Two things follow. Skimming is nearly four times more effective at the starting band than authored and saturates completely after one skim there, while the high band — where the design wants multi-pass descents to live — benefits least (11.8% off peak heat after three skims). The multipliers also move with entry depth: suborbital heat_vs_direct at one skim is 0.742 / 0.807 / 0.922 at the three sampled entry depths, so one global array cannot represent the effect at all.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"band_heat_ordering_contradicted_in_descents\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.7\",\n      \"claim\": \"ablation.heat_index asserts 73 / 100 / 138 for suborbital / low / high, derived from entry speed cubed times sqrt(beta), so the ride home gets hotter as the band rises.\",\n      \"measured\": \"The two sweep blocks disagree. In descents, full-hold peak heat falls as the band rises — 112 / 106 / 102 — with the solver choosing braking altitudes of 57952 / 53644.8 / 50903.8 m, i.e. the higher band enters deeper and still measures cooler, so that comparison is not controlled. In the depth-controlled skims block, at entry_depth 0 with an empty ship, peak heat runs 100 / 127.4 / 158.6 — a 1.59x spread that supports the design and beats the Researcher's 1.35x prediction. The design intent survives, but the authored 73 / 100 / 138 matches neither measurement, and difficulty_rises_with_band holds in only 0.383 of the grid.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"full_hold_touchdown_marginal_and_circular\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.2\",\n      \"claim\": \"landing.descent_speed_full_hold_ms asserts 4.6 m/s at full hold, comfortably under the 5 m/s soft-landing line, with a full hold at 1.95x dry mass (806 kg over six slots).\",\n      \"measured\": \"The params carry no canopy area, so the simulator back-solved 357.1 m2 from the 4.6 m/s claim itself — the descent-speed check is anchored to the number it is checking. With the catalog's own mass, 191.65 kg per slot and a 1149.9 kg full hold (2.35x dry mass, not 1.95x), every full-hold touchdown measures 4.99 m/s: soft by 0.01 m/s, at the starting band, before any parachute upgrade. Half hold is 4.21 and empty 3.25. full_hold_lands_soft holds in 0.29 of the grid.\",\n      \"severity\": \"significant\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ballistic_coefficient_near_the_aerobraking_floor\",\n      \"gdd_ref\": \"2.3.1\",\n      \"claim\": \"The Researcher's ballistic-coefficient check assumed 1400 kg staged and empty, giving beta = 267 kg/m2 and calling it comfortably above the 100 kg/m2 danger line.\",\n      \"measured\": \"As parameterised (dry_mass 850 kg, Cd_shield 1.5, area 3.5 m2) the flown staged beta is 161.9 kg/m2 and unstaged 485.7 — 39% below the figure the aerobraking arithmetic was built on, and only 3.2x above the ~50 kg/m2 floor where the atmosphere stops the ship instead of braking it. The grid's 7/8 configs sit at 133.3 to 1333.3. This is the quantity that controls whether skimming exists, and it is the one the crew never measured.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"kind\": \"tuning\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"proposed_changes\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.radius_m\",\n      \"current\": 250000,\n      \"proposed\": 60000,\n      \"reason\": \"Every config in the grid's top 12 sits at this radius and nowhere else, it is the only sampled radius where bands_reachable and fuel_margin_sane co-occur, and it collapses orbital periods from 44-80 minutes to single digits, which retires the Researcher's hard time-warp requirement; it costs the entire baseline derivation, which must be recomputed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.surface_gravity_ms2\",\n      \"current\": 4,\n      \"proposed\": 9.81,\n      \"reason\": \"All five 7/8 configs use it and the 6/8 configs at g=3 and g=6 all fail full_hold_lands_soft; the cost is that liftoff TWR collapses at the current thrust, which the next two changes pay for.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.thrust_n\",\n      \"current\": 12000,\n      \"proposed\": 48000,\n      \"reason\": \"At the proposed mass and gravity the present engine gives TWR 0.37 and cannot leave the pad; 48 kN restores roughly 1.5, and it is my arithmetic rather than a sweep measurement.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_burn_kgs\",\n      \"current\": 3.2,\n      \"proposed\": 12.8,\n      \"reason\": \"Holds exhaust velocity at 3750 m/s (Isp 382 s) through the thrust increase so the Delta-v budget stays honest; it quadruples burn rate, so tank sizing moves with it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.dry_mass_kg\",\n      \"current\": 850,\n      \"proposed\": 2400,\n      \"reason\": \"Raises staged beta from the measured 161.9 kg/m2 toward the 133-400 range the 7/8 configs occupy and is the mass every one of them flies; it makes the ship expensive to lift, which the thrust and tank changes absorb.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"flight.fuel_capacity_kg\",\n      \"current\": 450,\n      \"proposed\": 750,\n      \"reason\": \"At dry_mass 2400 and a ~950 m/s orbit-plus-losses budget on the small planet, 750 kg gives the mass ratio 1.29 that budget needs plus skim-shaping margin; the ascent failure was never diagnosed as tank-limited specifically, so this should be re-flown rather than trusted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.sea_level_density_kgm3\",\n      \"current\": 1,\n      \"proposed\": 1.2,\n      \"reason\": \"Together with reference_area 12 this is the single 7/8 config where skimming actually cools the entry ([1, 0.801, 0.299, 0.299]); it costs unstaged pass survivability outright (339 peak heat), which is the trade the grid says cannot be avoided.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.reentry.reference_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": 3.5,\n      \"proposed\": 12,\n      \"reason\": \"The other half of that config — it sets staged beta to 133.3 and is what makes the skim multipliers move at all; a wider ship also raises unstaged heating, which is the same cost named above.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.scale_height_m\",\n      \"current\": 6000,\n      \"proposed\": 1680,\n      \"reason\": \"The grid pairs this scale height and a 16800 m atmosphere top with every 60 km world it scored; leaving the old air column on the new planet would put the atmosphere above the bands.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"baseline.planet.atmosphere_top_m\",\n      \"current\": 78000,\n      \"proposed\": 16800,\n      \"reason\": \"Same pairing — ten scale heights, matching every scored config at this radius.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.cycle_toll_growth\",\n      \"current\": 1.9,\n      \"proposed\": 1,\n      \"reason\": \"This is GDD 4.5 risk 1's own named fallback: a flat per-pass toll. Compounding at 1.9 guarantees a single-pass optimum because the measured skim saving saturates (grid rate 0.889) while the toll does not, and no coefficient tuning fixes an affine-versus-geometric race; it costs the elegance of the U-curve and needs the pass cap below to keep feathering off the table.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.max_passes\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 4,\n      \"reason\": \"The second half of the same fallback — a hard cap replaces the anti-feathering job the growth term was doing, and it is a new field the schema does not yet have.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"ablation.skim_heat_multiplier\",\n      \"current\": [1, 0.94, 0.9, 0.88],\n      \"proposed\": [1, 0.801, 0.299, 0.299],\n      \"reason\": \"Replaces an admitted guess with the measured curve from the proposed world; it should become a per-band, per-depth table rather than a global array, because measurement shows it moves with both.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"landing.parachute_area_m2\",\n      \"current\": null,\n      \"proposed\": 357.1,\n      \"reason\": \"The simulator had to back-solve the canopy from descent_speed_full_hold_ms, so the landing check is currently circular; stating the area makes touchdown speed a measurement instead of a restatement. Both the economy-balancer and the sweep flagged this field as missing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"path\": \"reentry.heat_capacity\",\n      \"current\": 100,\n      \"proposed\": 120,\n      \"reason\": \"Full-hold suborbital peaks at 112 on its cheapest descent, so the starting loop damages cargo at the starting tier; 120 restores headroom at band one and the upgrade tiers (130, 165) should be re-spaced above it after the world change is re-flown.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_notes\": [\n    \"The two verification blocks disagree and I have leaned on one. The skims block fixes entry depth and compares bands cleanly (100 / 127.4 / 158.6 empty and direct); the descents block lets the solver choose braking altitude per case, so its inverted heat ordering (112 / 106 / 102) is an artifact of three different trajectories, not of the physics. The blocks also disagree on absolute scale — empty suborbital single-pass reads 100 in one and 71 in the other. Any finding of mine about band ordering should be re-checked against a single normalisation before anyone acts on it.\",\n    \"Every descent in the sweep was flown from an initial orbit the ship demonstrably cannot achieve, because all three ascents crashed with zero fuel. The descent findings are real statements about the reentry model and worthless as statements about a playable run until the ascent closes; fixing the ascent will change mass at entry and every heat number with it.\",\n    \"The full-hold touchdown speed is not an independent measurement. The simulator inferred a 357.1 m2 canopy from the params' own 4.6 m/s claim, so 4.99 m/s tests the cargo mass and nothing else. That the answer landed 0.01 m/s inside the soft line is coincidence, not margin.\",\n    \"Cargo mass is a flat 1149.9 kg in all three bands in this sweep, so the band-by-band mass gradient that the whole heat_index derivation rests on was never exercised. If high-band junk really is 403.9 kg per slot as the economy notes claim, every high-band descent here is roughly 1500 kg too light.\",\n    \"The exploration grid samples radius at 800, 60000, 160000 and 320000 m. There is nothing near the current 250000 and a factor-of-2.7 gap above 60000, so 'move to 60 km' may be over-fit to a coarse axis; a finer sweep between 60 and 160 km could well find something that keeps more of the Researcher's arithmetic intact.\",\n    \"The thrust and tank figures in my proposal are hand arithmetic against the proposed gravity and mass, not sweep output. The grid never varied thrust, burn rate or fuel capacity at all, so nothing in 324 configs confirms that the proposed world is flyable by any ship — only that its reentry targets are satisfiable.\",\n    \"Adopting the one 7/8 world where skimming works means accepting that an unstaged shallow pass burns (339 peak heat). That contradicts GDD 2.3.1's coarse-braking-before-staging sequence and should go to a human as a rules decision, not be absorbed as a tuning result. Staging stays one-way either way, so the pillar itself is untouched.\",\n    \"The simulator is a point mass with a perfect pilot: off_retrograde_penalty is 1, so no attitude error, no cosine heat penalty, no debris collisions, no chute-shred check against dynamic pressure, and no model of the Mach 3.7 deploy the Researcher flagged. It cannot say whether any of this is tense, and the plasma-to-chute window — the thing pillar three lives in — was not measured at all.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":206923,"ttft_stream_ms":7568,"time_to_request_ms":211,"type":"result","duration_ms":290165,"uuid":"05da96fa-ceb7-49ce-926b-548b7d0e0196"}
